    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d482">

                <pb facs="0581" n="1415" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1415"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/261c</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-19T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 19, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6940. Most urgent. We have been prepared since yesterday to take over Dutch ships
                    and cannot understand your failure to advise us either that we are free to take
                    this action or that an agreement has been reached in accordance with ultimatum
                    expiring on the 18th. We regard continued delay and uncertainty as very harmful
                    and we desire to take final action at once. Please give immediate reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
